# kernel.g
#
# Gappa proof of the kernel evaluation error of fixAsinExact / fixAcosExact.
#
# Method (src/exact/asin_acos.c, sollya/asin_acos.sollya): on the reduced interval
# [0, 1/2] asin is a degree-15 polynomial generated by Sollya fpminimax, with every
# coefficient stored as a Q61 fixed-point integer (c_i = round(p_i * 2^61)). The
# kernel is evaluated by Horner's rule in Q61 integer fixed point:
#
#     acc = (acc * x) >> 61 + c_i
#
# The arithmetic right shift on the signed 128-bit product is a truncation toward
# -infinity, i.e. the fixed rounding operator `fixed<61, dn>` in Gappa (downward
# rounding to multiples of 2^-61). One Horner step therefore loses exactly
#
#     r_i = fixed<61, dn>(a_{i+1} * x) - a_{i+1} * x   in  (-2^-61, 0],
#
# and the accumulated evaluation error e_i = s_i - p_i (computed versus exact
# polynomial) obeys the backward recurrence
#
#     e_15 = 0,   e_i = e_{i+1} * x + r_i,   e_0 = s_0 - p(x).
#
# Because each residue r_i lies in [-2^-61, 0] whatever the intermediate value, the
# recurrence decouples from the polynomial coefficients; Gappa proves a rigorous
# bound on |e_0| from the interval x in [0, 1/2] and the residue range alone.
#
# The polynomial-versus-function error is supplied as a certified hypothesis from
# sollya/asin_acos.out (supnorm of the quantised polynomial against asin over
# [0, 1/2]):
#
#     |p(x) - asin(x)| <= 6.17624436320711e-15
#
# so the total kernel error is bounded by that hypothesis plus the proved |e_0|.
# The design budget in docs/design/transcendentals.md is 6.19e-15 per function
# (asin and acos share this kernel on [0, 1/2]).

{
  x in [0, 0.5]

  /\ r15 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r14 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r13 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r12 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r11 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r10 in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r9  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r8  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r7  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r6  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r5  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r4  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r3  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r2  in [-4.34e-19, 0]
  /\ r1  in [-4.34e-19, 0]

  /\ e15 = 0
  /\ e14 = e15 * x + r15
  /\ e13 = e14 * x + r14
  /\ e12 = e13 * x + r13
  /\ e11 = e12 * x + r12
  /\ e10 = e11 * x + r11
  /\ e9  = e10 * x + r10
  /\ e8  = e9 * x + r9
  /\ e7  = e8 * x + r8
  /\ e6  = e7 * x + r7
  /\ e5  = e6 * x + r6
  /\ e4  = e5 * x + r5
  /\ e3  = e4 * x + r4
  /\ e2  = e3 * x + r3
  /\ e1  = e2 * x + r2
  /\ e0  = e1 * x + r1

  ->
  |e0| <= 9e-19 /\ |e0| + 6.17624436320711e-15 <= 6.19e-15
}
